BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2025 SFFSFF
DTSTART:20250607T220000Z
DTEND:20250608T002000Z
DTSTAMP:20250607T220000Z
UID:cYa66Ymf4a
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 120 mins (2h00m)\n\nA Cinematic Odyssey: 20 Years of
  Sci-Fi and Fantasy Shorts Celebrate 20 years of spellbinding cinema at th
 e Science Fiction and Fantasy Short Film Festival (SFFSFF) this June at SI
 FF Cinema Uptown. For two decades\, MoPOP and SIFF have put a spotlight on
  visionary filmmakers\, showcasing innovative short films that transport a
 udiences to brand-new worlds. The animated and live-action shorts are care
 fully curated and judged by a panel of film critics. Previous selections h
 ave transcended the screen\, earning international distribution\, Academy 
 Award nominations\, museum exhibitions\, and more.  Join us this summer f
 or captivating screenings\, a filmmaker Q&A\, and an awards ceremony as we
  celebrate 20 years of groundbreaking cinema and fearless storytelling. Ju
 ne 7 Tickets: $22 SIFF Members\, MoPOP Members\, Students | $24 RegularJu
 ne 7 Screenings: Block 1 & 2 Films June 8 Tickets: $12 SIFF Members\, MoP
 OP Members | $17 Students | $18 RegularJune 8 Screenings: Day 2 Films (Nex
 t Generation Filmmakers)\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/sffsf
 f-x37750
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:High Art
DTSTART:20250607T233000Z
DTEND:20250608T013500Z
DTSTAMP:20250607T233000Z
UID:C4tB5daYJV
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nAt 24\, Syd (Radha Mitchell) has
  landed what seems to be a dream job but she’s still stuck fetching coff
 ee\, until a chance meeting with her upstairs neighbor\, Lucy Berlinerr (A
 lly Sheedy). Lucy\, a once-celebrated photographer\, lives an enthralling 
 life with her drug-addicted German girlfriend\, (Patricia Clarkson)\, that
  draws Syd in. Before she can catch her breath\, Syd discovers dark truths
  of life on the edge\, is forced to confont the price of her hunger for re
 cognition and public esteem.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/hi
 gh-art
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
